-- title:
--   Anchoring label for the semistable covering at q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and suppose $M'$ is divisible by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$, and let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places, that is, of the rational affine geometric places at which the geometric $j$-value lies in `ssJSet q`. Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the former along $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$, whose residue map is computed coefficientwise on Laurent series with coefficients in $A$. Fix $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and two families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The hypotheses on these are: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ is the ring of quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator has nonzero reduction; each $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(L)$ is the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \infty = L$; $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; every level automorphism $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ by pullback; each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ exactly in $A$, is stable under pullback by all such level automorphisms, contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for every $a \in A$, and dominates $R_0$ in the sense that for $f \in R_0$'s integers regular wherever $j_q$ is, whose residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and $f - a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ whenever the residue of $a \in A$ equals the value of $R_0$'s residue of $f$ at $s$. Finally let $\mathcal{C}$ be a semistable covering for $(q, M', A, W)$ such that the integers of each Igusa chart $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,L$ equal $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(L)$; such that for $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, equality of the integers of $(\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,L).\mathrm{comap}\,\tau$ and of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,L$ forces equality of their domains; such that any permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ realising the pullback action of $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ on the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ also matches the domains and moduli of the annuli $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{An}$; and such that $\mathcal{C}$ satisfies `EquivClauses`. Then there is a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta_0$ such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every line $L$, the pullback of $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,L$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta_0\,\gamma^{-1}$ has the same integers and the same domain as $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{CIg}\,((\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma)^{-1} \cdot L)$, and for every $s \in W$ the pullback of the annulus $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{An}\,L\,s$ along the same automorphism has the same domain as $\mathcal{C}.\mathrm{An}\,((\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma)^{-1} \cdot L)\,s$.
--
--   This is the naturality clause that pins down the labelling of the Igusa components of the semistable covering of the modular curve attached to $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ in the case $q = 3$: for one choice of the root-of-unity label $\zeta_0$, the permutation of components and tube annuli induced by a level automorphism at $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ is exactly the inverse of the action of the reduction of $\gamma$ on $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$. It is used by the existence theorem for semistable coverings with the equivariance clauses, `exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd`, and relies on the Borel stability of the Gauss ring at $q = 3$ together with the composition law for the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$.
